agent-ops task task-697f067b-a9f4-490e-8e11-9ee864a2af5f: Escape Loop R1 record: receipt v2, origin gate, linking, ledger
intent: R1 of the Escape Loop per the fixed goal; R2 (rules file, replay proof, backtest, --escape-fix, agent-ops escapes) stays out. Receipt schema v2 adds commits (target..candidate) and per-file diff fingerprints; readers accept v1/v2. New runtime/src/escape module: link resolution (override, range, fingerprint, unresolved reason, ungated), earliest-gate label with mechanical git grep -F replay of the linked receipt's surface queries (surface-excluded/surface-unseen override a later agent label), blame hints via git blame argv at base, ledger writer. Origin is an optional AgentTask field bound into taskContractHash; DEBUG tasks created after this change carry originRequired and need task debug --debug-action origin (after a confirmed hypothesis, inside the DEBUG budget) before completion (ESCAPE_ORIGIN_MISSING); normal tasks opt in with task create --escape-of/--escape-receipt/--escape-label. Ledger: one tracked data-only JSON per task under .agent-ops-escapes/ (merge-safe). gate-catch local-log events {code, taskId}, fail-open. Review packet and prompt carry escape data to both rounds. Spec en+zh-TW and managed DEBUG text. Zero new dependencies; git via argv only.
criteria:
- ac1-receipt-v2: Finish receipts are written as schemaVersion 2 carrying every commit in target..candidate and a per-file diff fingerprint (path plus sha256 of the normalized per-file diff, stable across squash); review-show and every receipt reader accept v1 and v2; a v1 receipt still loads and links only by exact candidateHead; on a synthetic repo a squash-merged commit of a receipt's range links to that receipt by fingerprint (checks escape-receipt-v2, escape-receipt-v1-compat, escape-squash-fingerprint); the runner's 26 pre-existing startup/surface checks keep passing.
- ac2-origin-gate: A DEBUG task created after this change cannot complete (task complete / worktree finish / completion gate) until an origin is declared, failing with ESCAPE_ORIGIN_MISSING; origin (escape-of <commit> with agent label | pre-existing + reason | external + reason) is declared via task debug --debug-action origin only after a confirmed hypothesis (ESCAPE_ORIGIN_EARLY otherwise), within the DEBUG budget, and is bound into taskContractHash; tasks without origin keep their old hash; normal tasks accept optional task create --escape-of <commit> [--escape-receipt <id>] [--escape-label <label>]; the declaration output lists git blame hint commits for the fix's changed/removed lines at the base (checks escape-origin-required, escape-origin-contract, escape-blame-hints).
- ac3-link-label: An escape-of commit resolves in order: --escape-receipt override, commit inside a receipt's recorded range (v1: exact head), per-file fingerprint match, else unresolved with a reason (receipt-not-local when a Git note names a missing receipt, no-matching-receipt, ambiguous-receipt) or ungated when no local receipt or note exists; the primary label is the earliest gate (requirement, surface, scenario, criteria, verify, review, flagged, out-of-model) and git grep -F replay of the linked receipt's recorded surface queries at the escaped candidate marks the fix's files surface-excluded (matched an exclusion) or surface-unseen (no query hit, not included), overriding a later agent label; label, agent label, mechanical facts and the linked receipt's residual risks appear in both review rounds' packet/prompt (checks escape-link-states, escape-surface-replay, escape-review-packet).
- ac4-ledger-events: Each declared escape writes exactly one data-only record (task id, escape commit, link state and reason, receipt id, labels, missed paths, residual-risk count; no file contents or transcripts) under the git-tracked .agent-ops-escapes/ directory as one file per task, re-declaration replaces it; gate catch events (SURFACE_* and SCENARIO_MISSING review blocks, review FAIL, verify FAIL-to-PASS on a task) append local-log events of type gate-catch carrying only code and taskId, and a logging failure never changes the gate result (checks escape-ledger, escape-catch-events).
- ac5-spec: docs/en/spec and docs/zh-TW/spec define the origin declaration and escape linking clause (link states, resolution order, labels, ledger, R1 scope) and the managed .agent-ops CLAUDE.md/AGENTS.md DEBUG text requires origin before review; docs and install tests in npm test pass (check escape-spec-docs).
